Target

The target column is Employability.

The target contains three values:

High
Medium
Low

How the Entries Were Created

Each row represents one CSE student.

The dataset contains the student's CGPA, technical skills, soft skills, internship, certifications, projects and placement training information.

The Employability column is used as the target for the machine learning model.

3. Preprocessing

The Excel dataset is loaded using pandas.

Duplicate rows are removed.

Numerical columns are converted into numerical values.

If any numerical value is missing, it is filled using the median value of that column.

Missing values in Internship and PlacementTraining are filled with No.

The Employability column is also checked for missing values.

After preprocessing, the cleaned data is used for feature engineering.

4. Feature Engineering

Feature engineering is used to create useful features from the existing student data.

The features used in the Feast FeatureView are:

cgpa – Student's CGPA

programming – Programming skill

dsa – DSA skill

dbms – DBMS skill

os – Operating Systems skill

cn – Computer Networks skill

python – Python skill

java – Java skill

webdevelopment – Web development skill

ai_ml – AI and Machine Learning skill

cloud – Cloud computing skill

devops – DevOps skill

cybersecurity – Cybersecurity skill

communication – Communication skill

aptitude – Aptitude skill

teamwork – Teamwork skill

certifications – Number of certifications

projects – Number of projects

technical_skill_average – Average of the 12 technical skills

soft_skill_average – Average of Communication, Aptitude and Teamwork

experience_score – Score based on internship, placement training, certifications and projects

overall_skill_score – Overall score based on technical and soft skills

Technical Skill Average

The Technical Skill Average is calculated using the 12 technical skills.

Technical Skill Average =

(Programming + DSA + DBMS + OS + CN + Python + Java + WebDevelopment + AI_ML + Cloud + DevOps + CyberSecurity) / 12

For example, if the total technical skill score is 80:

Technical Skill Average = 80 / 12

Technical Skill Average = 6.67

Soft Skill Average

The Soft Skill Average is calculated using Communication, Aptitude and Teamwork.

Soft Skill Average =

(Communication + Aptitude + Teamwork) / 3

Experience Score

The Experience Score is calculated using internship, placement training, certifications and projects.

For Internship and PlacementTraining:

Yes = 1

No = 0

Experience Score = Internship + Placement Training + Certifications + Projects

Overall Skill Score

The Overall Skill Score is calculated using the technical skill average and soft skill average.

Overall Skill Score =

(Technical Skill Average + Soft Skill Average) / 2

5. Difference Between Original Dataset and Feature Dataset

The original dataset contains complete information about the students.

It includes student details, CGPA, technical skills, soft skills, internship, certifications, projects, placement training and employability.

The feature dataset contains the values needed for Feast and the machine learning model.

New features are also created from the original columns:

Technical Skill Average

Soft Skill Average

Experience Score

Overall Skill Score

The final feature data is saved as a Parquet file.

