7. Implementation

Entity

The entity used in this project is Student.

StudentID is used to uniquely identify each student.

Entity name: student

Entity key: student_id

Data Source

After feature engineering, the data is saved in Parquet format.

The file used as the Feast data source is student_features.parquet.

This file is used as the offline data source.

FeatureView

The FeatureView is named student_skill_features.

It contains the student's CGPA, technical skills, soft skills, certifications, projects and calculated features.

Registration Using feast apply

The Feast objects are registered using the feast apply command.

This registers the entity, data source and FeatureView with Feast.

Historical Feature Retrieval

Historical features are retrieved using get_historical_features().

The historical features are taken from the offline data and used for training the machine learning model.

Machine Learning Model

A Random Forest Classifier is used as the machine learning model.

The model uses the features retrieved from Feast to predict the student's employability.

The possible predictions are:

High
Medium
Low

The Employability column is used as the target and is not given as an input feature to the model.

Materialization

The features are materialized from the offline store into the online store.

The online store used in this project is SQLite.

Materialization makes the feature values available for online retrieval.

Online Feature Retrieval

Online features are retrieved using get_online_features().

The StudentID is used to retrieve the features of a particular student.

These retrieved features are then given to the trained machine learning model to make the final prediction.

