10. Conclusion

In this project, the CSE Employability Dataset was first cleaned and prepared for use.

Feature engineering was then performed to create useful features such as Technical Skill Average, Soft Skill Average, Experience Score and Overall Skill Score.

The processed data was saved as Parquet data and used in Feast.

A Student entity was created using StudentID. A data source and FeatureView were also created. The Feast objects were registered using feast apply.

Historical features were retrieved from the offline data and used to train a Random Forest classification model.

The features were then materialized into the SQLite online store. Online features were retrieved using StudentID and given to the trained model.

The model achieved 95.00% accuracy, and the prediction for StudentID 1 was High.

This project demonstrates the complete process of using Feast with a simple machine learning model, from preprocessing the dataset to retrieving features and making the final prediction.
